"""Apply final review's explicit goal-duration and frozen-actor contract."""
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(__file__).with_name('mechanism.html');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
s=s.replace('last_progress_time}</code>','last_progress_time, evaluation_end_time, achieved}</code>')
s=s.replace('Reconsider every 0.5 s, immediately on harm, or after 2 s without measured progress toward the desired relationship.', 'For the initial qualification design, retain the selected relationship for a six-second evaluation period. Check its validity and progress every 0.5 s and immediately on harm. Reaching the required hold marks it achieved; continue comparing movements that maintain that same relationship until the evaluation period ends. This is a generic relationship-maintenance choice, not a fixed hand pose or a named grasp routine. Ordinary goal replacement occurs at the end of that period. After 2 s without progress, widen the allowed search variations within the existing physical envelope; do not fabricate a new successful-goal label. Six seconds is an explicit design setting, not an infant timing claim.')
s=s.replace('If identity becomes ambiguous, keep the intention but suspend object-directed closure; reacquire the object or choose the existing protective/exploration path.', 'If identity becomes ambiguous, suspend object-directed closure and end this goal-evaluation period as an identity-loss event; reacquire the object through the existing protective/exploration path. Record the retained intention for possible later reacquisition under a new period, never silently continue its old value window.')
s=s.replace('The initial total comparison horizon is six seconds: three seconds explicitly forecast and a three-second learned continuation.', 'At the start of an intention period, the total comparison horizon is six seconds: three seconds explicitly forecast and a three-second learned continuation. Later choices clip the horizon to the time remaining in that same period. Set explicit duration L=min(3 s, remaining time) and continuation H=remaining time-L. Use the equation below with 3 s replaced by L, state 60 replaced by the last explicit row, and value duration 3 s replaced by H. When H is zero there is no continuation term.')
s=s.replace('Use h of 0.5, 1, 2 or 3 seconds.', 'Use h in 50 ms increments up to three seconds, including 0.5, 1, 2 and 3 seconds. Record targets from the actual timestamped readings for each requested duration; do not interpolate an unobserved return.')
s=s.replace('Only windows in which that same intention g was actually retained and the specified behavior policy ran can teach this goal-conditioned value.', 'Only windows in which that same intention g was actually retained and the specified behavior policy ran can teach this goal-conditioned value. Successful completion keeps that relationship active for the rest of its evaluation period, so early success still supplies later maintenance windows. Both successes and failures enter the dataset.')
s=s.replace('Pin the behavior policy, representation, raw-channel normalization and weight version.', 'Freeze the acting chooser, forward predictors, encoder, value heads, raw-channel normalization and weights for one collection epoch. Train candidate copies offline from collected data; promote a candidate only between epochs after qualification. This prevents each optimizer update from changing the behavior being measured. Pin those versions in every record.')
s=s.replace('A true completed physical episode has no tail.', 'The value target here counts utility while this goal-evaluation period is active, not unlimited lifetime utility. At its scheduled end the finite horizon is exhausted. Harm requiring a protective stop or loss of object identity ends the period early: include all actually observed channel values and harm through that event, then define the remaining goal-period utility and potential to be zero. This is an explicit task-period terminal condition, not a claim that the physical world ended. Save the reason and include the terminated window for every supported requested h; never drop only unsuccessful periods. Normal goal achievement does not terminate the period early. A true completed physical episode likewise has no tail.')
s=s.replace('A physical fault records actual harm and ends that episode.', 'A physical fault records actual harm and ends the physical episode as well as the goal period. A logging or process failure with missing observations is different: retain it as incomplete evidence, do not fill the missing interval with zeros, and report its count separately from physical failures.')
s=s.replace('keep a variance floor of 0.01 of its allowed range', 'keep a standard-deviation floor of 0.01 of its allowed range')
s=s.replace('Reconsidering all four outcomes costs at most 7,680 forecasts; do that only at the 0.5 s reconsideration boundary or an invalidation.', 'Comparing all four outcomes costs at most 7,680 forecasts; do that when choosing a new six-second intention period after the previous period ends. During a period the 0.5 s checks keep the same relationship or end it on harm/identity loss; they do not change its value target.')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
print('Goal period and acting version boundaries specified')
